\details{
Each row is one product. Required means there is no default. Omitted optional
fields take the default shown.

Explicit missing values are accepted only where
stated. Numeric fields accept integer or double input. Whole-number fields
reject fractional values.

Logical fields also accept numeric zero and one. Factors are converted for character fields.
Bounds use the stated endpoint
convention.

Equality of an inclusive lower and exclusive upper bound leaves
no eligible entry value.

Length means feet with imperial calls and meters with metric calls. Diameter means inches or
centimeters. Product definitions initially normalize lengths to the nearest inch, with
halves upward, and retain the original supplied values.

Merchandising normalizes those values to one inch or 0.0254 meter under the selected units.
Preserve product attributes so metric calls use the original specifications. Selecting
metric units does not convert measurements supplied in feet or inches.

Board-foot procedures still measure in inches and feet.

Tree entry requires the relevant species, age, and pruning measurements. Missing required
attributes can produce \code{missing_product_attribute}. Diameter at breast height
limits choose the entry product.

Later use requires
\code{allow_after_higher_product} and still checks species, age, and pruning. Log diameters are
tested at the physical endpoints, including trim at the small
end. A missing optional upper limit imposes no limit, not a zero limit.

