\section{Compatibility}{
Former fields are accepted for migration with deprecation messages. \code{fallback},
\code{pulp_product}, \code{max_defect_pct},
\code{price_quantity}, and \code{source_id} map to
\code{allow_after_higher_product}, \code{accepts_pulp_restriction},
\code{max_rot_pct}, \code{price_per}, and \code{specification_source}. \code{grade} becomes
\code{meta_grade}.

The package does not assign grades. \code{min_top_length}, \code{continue_to_top}, and
\code{max_pieces} map to
\code{min_boundary_length}, \code{allow_lower_products}, and
\code{max_logs_per_segment}.

The former \code{sold_by} and \code{diameter_basis} fields map to the measurement
fields described in \link[=scaling_rules]{Scaling rules}. The former rounding
columns are accepted only in additional reporting definitions. \code{length_parity} is
translated into explicit lengths or a range.

\code{segmentation_policy} belongs to \code{\link{products_from_nvel_rules}}
and the recorded source settings, not an authored specification. }
\section{Status and missing values}{
Invalid specifications stop the call. The checked table has no calculation status codes. A
valid specification does not guarantee volume.

See \link[=result_tables]{Result tables} for
statuses and missing result quantities. }
